# Files that are executed by Linux (in the training container / on a rented GPU) must keep
# LF endings in the WORKING COPY, not only in the repository.
#
# Why this file exists: core.autocrlf=true on this machine, and container_export.tar.gz is
# packed from the working copy — so a CRLF preflight.sh ships to the instance and bash dies
# on the first line with `$'\r': command not found` / `invalid option name: set: pipefail`.
# `git apply` likewise rejects a patch whose lines end in CRLF.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.patch         text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.dockerignore  text eol=lf

# Belt and braces now that a 14 MB PDF is tracked. Git already auto-detects this,
# so it changes nothing today -- it just makes the intent explicit.
*.pdf           binary
